  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "R13 and R15 establish accurate, computationally efficient MTPs for the closely related BCC MoNbTaW refractory alloy, while R5 and R11 show that interatomic potentials can capture SRO and that SRO materially changes energetics in refractory HEAs. R1, R2, R7, R14, R19, and R20 further indicate that finite-temperature electronic, magnetic, and entropic free-energy contributions can shift phase behavior. However, none of the records proposes a liquid-phase MTP as the reference for DFT free energies, replacing thermodynamic integration with free-energy perturbation, or exploiting the small MTP–DFT energy-difference variance. They also do not connect a Fermi-level DOS gap and SRO stabilization quantitatively to melting-temperature shifts. Thus the records point toward accurate MTP-based thermodynamics and relevant free-energy corrections, but the combined MTP–FEP melting workflow requires a substantial additional idea."
